<title>UK: RUGBY UNION-BRIVE WIN EUROPEAN CUP.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-BRIVE WIN EUROPEAN CUP.</headline>
<dateline>CARDIFF 1997-01-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brive beat Leicester 28-9 (halftime 8-6) in the European Cup rugby union final at Cardiff Arms Park on Saturday:</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Brive - Tries: Sebastien Viars, Gerald Fabre, Sebastien Carrat (2). Conversion: Christophe Lamaison. Penalty: Lamaison. Drop-goal: Lamaison.</p>
<p>Leicester - Penalties: John Liley (3).</p>
<p>Attendance: 40,664.</p>
</text>
